; Not steps after the first: a multiset store.  Under step every, copy's
; match reads (a), which is there from the start, and each step makes one
; more copy of (b): in a multiset store a firing that makes a row again is a
; step.  Meeting only the matches that read a fresh row would stop after one
; copy, so this program's steps meet every match, until the budget is spent.
(store multiset)
(step every)
(budget 4)
(a)
(rule copy (read (a)) (make (b)))
